- **Validate and sanitize user IDs**: Ensure `userId` contains only alphanumeric characters and hyphens using a regex like `^[a-zA-Z0-9-]+$`, rejecting any special characters that could enable URL injection.  
- **URL-encode concatenated values**: Use `encodeURIComponent(userId)` to safely append `userId` to `apiUrl`, preventing malicious path manipulation (e.g., `../etc/passwd`).  
- **Reject invalid input strictly**: Return `null` for empty strings or invalid IDs, ensuring no malformed URLs are generated.  

```javascript
function getUrlForQuery(apiUrl, userId) {
  if (!userId || !/^[a-zA-Z0-9-]+$/.test(userId)) {
    return null;
  }
  return `${apiUrl}${encodeURIComponent(userId)}`;
}
